sprdbt_tty on an SDIO WCN bus: four framing defects

sprdbt_tty comes from the realme tree as tty-pcie and is written for the PCIe/EDMA
transport. This board's WCN is on SDIO, and three of its assumptions do not hold. All three
are inside the driver, so none of them touch Wi-Fi (which uses its own channel path).

1. BT_RX_DMA_SIZE 2048 exceeds what the SDIO bus will carry.

   sdiohal sizes the TX half of every push as SDIOHAL_ALIGN_4BYTE(mbuf->len + sizeof(struct
   bus_puh_t)) and refuses anything above MAX_PAC_SIZE = SDIOHAL_BLK_SIZE * 2 = 840 * 2 =
   1680. Pushing an RX buffer with len = 2048 asks for 2052:

       WCN SDIO: pac size > cp buf size,len 2052
       WCN SDIO: sdio adma write fail ret:-1

   The first failure also sets the WCN carddump flag, and start_marlin() then refuses to
   power the BT function for the rest of the boot:

       WCN SDIO: carddump flag set[1]
       bluetooth_set_power: end_block: 0, ret: -1
       mtty_open : set power failed , return!

   The RX allocation has to stay at the full 1680 because the RX side of the sg list is
   built with MAX_PAC_SIZE regardless of the mbuf length, but only 1680 - 4 = 1676 bytes
   may be described by the header.

2. BT_SDIO_HEAD_LEN 0 lets the bus header overwrite the HCI command.

   sdiohal_tx_fill_puh() writes the 4-byte bus_puh_t at mbuf->buf[0] while mtty_write()
   memcpy'd the HCI data there too, so the first four bytes of every command (the H4 type
   and the opcode) were replaced by type/subtype/len/eof. The controller therefore received
   a packet that was not a valid HCI command. Reserve the four bytes on TX and strip them on
   RX.

3. mtty_rx_cb() used head->len, which is not the payload length on SDIO.

   sdiohal_rx_list_parser() assigns mbuf->len = MAX_MBUF_SIZE before handing the buffer up
   and never copies the length the chip wrote into the bus_puh_t, so head->len is 2048 for
   every packet. Passing that to tty_insert_flip_string() fed hci_uart a whole zero-filled
   buffer; it logged "Frame reassembly failed (-84)" on repeat and the tty reported ~20 MB
   of RX with zero parsed events. The real length is the header's len field, bits 7..22.

Verified on the NX302J after the three changes, with the controller powered and btattach
attached: "pac size > cp buf" no longer appears, bluetooth_set_power returns 0, mtty_open
succeeds, and hciconfig reports RX bytes:0 with no reassembly errors - the garbage flood is
gone. The controller still does not answer HCI (TX 1 command, RX 0 events), which is a
separate transport question and is recorded in the progress document.

--- a/tty-pcie/tty.h
+++ b/tty-pcie/tty.h
@@ -33,9 +33,12 @@
 #define BT_TX_POOL_SIZE0   64  // the max buffer is 64
 #define BT_TX_POOL_SIZE1   64
 #define BT_RX_POOL_SIZE   1
-#define BT_SDIO_HEAD_LEN   0
+/* the SDIO bus puts a bus_puh_t in front of the payload on both directions */
+#define BT_SDIO_HEAD_LEN   4
 #define BT_RX_MAX_NUM 4
-#define BT_RX_DMA_SIZE 2048
+/* the RX sg list is built with MAX_PAC_SIZE (840 * 2), so the allocation must reach it;
+ * only the part the header can describe is pushed */
+#define BT_RX_DMA_SIZE 1680

 #endif

--- a/tty-pcie/tty.c
+++ b/tty-pcie/tty.c
@@ -171,7 +171,7 @@
 		mbuf->phy = (unsigned long)(temp.phy);
         dm_rx_phy[i] = mbuf->phy;
-		mbuf->len = temp.size;
-		memset(mbuf->buf, 0x0, mbuf->len);
+		mbuf->len = temp.size - BT_SDIO_HEAD_LEN;
+		memset(mbuf->buf, 0x0, temp.size);
 		mbuf = mbuf->next;
 	}

@@ -278,7 +278,10 @@
-    len_send = head->len;
+    /* head->len is MAX_MBUF_SIZE whatever the chip wrote; the real length is the len field
+     * of the bus_puh_t the bus left at buf[0] (bits 7..22). */
+    len_send = (*(unsigned int *)head->buf >> 7) & 0xffff;

@@ -486,7 +489,8 @@
-        tx_head->buf = (unsigned char *)dma_alloc_coherent(dm, count, (dma_addr_t *)(&(tx_head->phy)), GFP_DMA);
+        /* keep room for the bus_puh_t the SDIO bus writes at buf[0] */
+        tx_head->buf = (unsigned char *)dma_alloc_coherent(dm, count + BT_SDIO_HEAD_LEN, (dma_addr_t *)(&(tx_head->phy)), GFP_DMA);

@@ -494,7 +498,7 @@
-        memcpy(tx_head->buf, buf, count);
+        memcpy(tx_head->buf + BT_SDIO_HEAD_LEN, buf, count);

@@ -503,7 +507,7 @@
-            dma_free_coherent(dm, count, (void *)tx_head->buf, tx_head->phy);
+            dma_free_coherent(dm, count + BT_SDIO_HEAD_LEN, (void *)tx_head->buf, tx_head->phy);
